/*!
   \qmlmodule org.kde.kirigamiaddons.components
   \title Kirigami Addons Components QML Types
   \brief Reusable controls and visual components for Kirigami applications.

   Use \l Avatar to represent a person with a profile image, initials, or
   an icon. \l ConvergentContextMenu presents actions as a menu on desktop
   and as a bottom drawer on mobile. \l MessageDialog displays success,
   warning, error, and information messages, with an optional "Don't show
   again" choice. \l FloatingToolBar places tools over content, while
   \l FloatingButton and \l DoubleFloatingButton provide prominent page
   actions.

   Import the module in the QML files that use these components:

   \qml
   import org.kde.kirigamiaddons.components as Components

   Components.Avatar {
       name: i18nc("@info:person", "Alex Doe")
   }
   \endqml
*/

/*!
   \qmlmodule org.kde.kirigamiaddons.labs.components
   \title Kirigami Addons Components (Labs) QML Types
   \brief Additional components for specialized interfaces.

   The labs module contains additional components for specialized
   interfaces, including media viewing. Import it separately when using
   those types:

   \qml
   import org.kde.kirigamiaddons.labs.components as LabsComponents
   \endqml
*/
